{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558334-mixing-god-bonding-with-technocratic-hypertech","id":1558334,"title":"Mixing God-Bonding with Technocratic Hypertech","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-02-14T17:23:07-08:00","id":1558334,"title":"Mixing God-Bonding with Technocratic Hypertech","content":"The following may be a bit of a stretch.<br /> <br /> As my profile picture indicates, I am a big fan of <i>Shin Megami Tensei</i> and I had this idea for a Technocracy character based on the most recent installment to the franchise, <i>Shin Megami Tensei V</i>. In the very beginning of the game, the protagonist fuses with a &quot;proto-fiend&quot; and gains the potential for godlike power. To avoid overexplaining and spoiling the game, this proto-fiend is just like the other demons presented throughout the game, figures from an array of different mythologies, with the distinction that he's a form of artificial life.<br /> <br /> Getting back to Mage, one practice described in <i>Book of Secrets</i> reminded me of this event of the game in particular: the practice of God-bonding in which the mage does magick by incorporating characteristics of a divine patron (maybe to a certain extent, becoming said patron). Now, everything in the section describing the practice screams that it's best suited for your mystical mages, be it from the Traditions, Disparates or independent Crafts (Marauders are even mentioned to prefer this practice). All the associated paradigms, abilities and instruments are ubiquitous in the descriptions for these types of mages. But... what if a technocrat could also employ God-bonding?<br /> <br /> Unmutual, I know, but hear me out. Some of the associated paradigms with God-bonding are found in the Technocracy, mainly &quot;Everything's an Illusion&quot; (even though the examples given by <i>Technocracy Reloaded </i>tend to substitute &quot;illusion&quot; for &quot;data&quot;) and &quot;A World of Gods and Monsters&quot; (even though this one is mainly a paradigm for the Void Engineers). For abilities, Cosmology could be used by a Void Engineer and Medicine is a given for a Progenitor. Instruments are more difficult to define for this concept, but blood is a frequent one for Progenitors and weapons are easy to associate with any convention. The necessity of faith for the practice shouldn't be a problem, since both <i>Guide to The Technocracy</i> and <i>Technocracy Reloaded</i> dictates that faith is a matter for individual agents to define for themselves.<br /> <br /> So, let's say this character (probably a Progenitor or Void Engineer), by using Dimensional Science, manages to contact a god-form manifested in their own religious beliefs, binds them to a type of alien hypertech and now uses this Venom-like armor to enact their Procedures. Is this rationale even possible? How much of a Reality Deviance is this character commiting and how would a technocract explain all of this in the line of Enlightned Science?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28986-agrat","name":"Agrat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28986_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-14T17:52:27-08:00","id":1558336,"title":"","content":"They would likely do it to something from the Digital Web, or something like a Tech Sprint and bond it to a H.I.T Mark or a Cyborg, heck in 1e I think there was a Rote that effectively did the same thing. Void Engineers may get Umberal and the Progenitors may play with a Sprint already bound to something in the material world like a Gestalt entity bound to somthing, Heck the N.W.O may have a Gestalt Entity already on leash that they spreed through 4-Chan, Q-Anon, Twitter/X, &quot;Truth Social&quot; or Joe Rogan Podcasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12939-clive-coursor","name":"Clive Coursor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-15T02:19:27-08:00","id":1558341,"title":"","content":"Consider the Syndicate; they have a division that experiments with merging Extra-dimensional Entities with people to grant them superhuman powers: the Special Projects Division. There's no reference to religion here; just a practical exploitation of a known type of inhuman entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-15T13:54:23-08:00","id":1558344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558334-mixing-god-bonding-with-technocratic-hypertech?p=1558341#post1558341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consider the Syndicate; they have a division that experiments with merging Extra-dimensional Entities with people to grant them superhuman powers: the Special Projects Division. There's no reference to religion here; just a practical exploitation of a known type of inhuman entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Syndicate would cut its deals with Mammon, Plutus or some other God of Wealth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T00:16:03-07:00","id":1562031,"title":"","content":"Perfectly acceptable as long as you keep it centered on science: there's no such a thing as a scientifically reachable god, but there are alien entities from other dimensions that can be studied and experimented upon.<br /> <br /> That is, just slap &quot;alien&quot; over &quot;god&quot; and call it a day, no one will think you're unmutual just because you're exploring a phenomenon that's demonstrably real. Just don't use superstitious explanations.<br /> <br /> As for what each Convention could do, that depends on how you want to use the proto-fiend. My suggestion: it should be a cross-convention project with a select user. Aogami could be represented by a combination of Avatar, Ally and Device plus some interesting Merits and be your main Instrument.<br /> <br /> You'll have a hard time making a Nahobino that is the creator of the artificial god and justify their Magic coming from it, but something closer to the original story is actually feasible, and something a very weird group within the Union could do. It's the kind of thing that needs know-how from every Convention: a spirit that's also a cyborg, with a psyche both complete and capable of fusing with another, the mix of Ephemera and metal is also capable of fusing with and altering a biological body, and Value is the Energy-Concept that seals the fusion better than regular Primal Energy could.<br /> <br /> Such a character would not be allowed in any mission, though. Being more subtle than a HIT-Mark V isn't a high bar, so they're for a game with focus on Du'at, I mean, in the Umbra. It's otherwise doable with starting points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}